ulty":1,"explanation":"Bonsai trees are kept small through techniques such as pruning and root restriction; they are not a naturally tiny species.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-711f-8dc0-ed86bee15b3f","description":"Bonsai","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7277-b12d-7eb467dc2d81","description":"Ornamental Shrubbery","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7bc5-9ea0-84cb53286ffb","description":"Decorage","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7d33-b2df-10f47771af58","description":"Topiary","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-751f-899e-d5d61251d090","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"How often do we usually have leap years?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Every four years, February gets a 29th day to keep the calendar aligned with Earth\u2019s roughly 365\u00bc-day orbit. Century years are exceptions unless divisible by 400.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7c54-b41d-e3bef32e1561","description":"Every four years","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7934-8860-a145683c3a41","description":"Every two years","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-796b-904f-47f3be482bd0","description":"Every six years","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7fe0-8e8b-68a56ab3bd78","description":"Every year","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-72f4-8c5f-b391ceffc1fe","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What type of comparison is the phrase \'He was like an eagle chained to the ground\' an example of?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A simile makes an explicit comparison using \u201clike\u201d or \u201cas\u201d; a metaphor states that one thing is another.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-7ecd-9c43-033802c3982a","description":"A simile","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-70b2-9446-6aa4a3879295","description":"A metaphor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ef-701c-87e9-ff83ba6f4579","description":"An allegory","cor